  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 7.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "right, thanks for waiting, come in. So, what would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.45,
      "end_seconds": 14.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "well, I've been having a chesty cough for a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 15.83,
      "end_seconds": 27.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 73 beats a minute, blood pressure 116 over 68. Respiratory rate 15, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.13,
      "end_seconds": 28.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.15,
      "end_seconds": 49.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.83,
      "end_seconds": 54.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "About... well, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.46,
      "end_seconds": 58.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Is it it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.09,
      "end_seconds": 63.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.84,
      "end_seconds": 67.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Any a sore throat earlier as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.64,
      "end_seconds": 82.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.42,
      "text": "yes, for six months as for sore throat earlier, a three out of ten, I suppose erm, I've also had slight aching"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.12,
      "end_seconds": 92.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Have you had a chesty cough for a week before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.65,
      "end_seconds": 100.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.1,
      "end_seconds": 105.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "let me check a few things any fever or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.34,
      "end_seconds": 110.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "None of those, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.2,
      "end_seconds": 116.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any breathlessness or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.71,
      "end_seconds": 121.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Let me think, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.36,
      "end_seconds": 126.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "okay, anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.04,
      "end_seconds": 129.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.23,
      "end_seconds": 144.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.04,
      "end_seconds": 159.95,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. No, I've never smoked in my life. I live with my elderly mother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.0,
      "end_seconds": 164.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.89,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.83,
      "end_seconds": 177.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.05,
      "end_seconds": 183.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "I'm on simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.63,
      "end_seconds": 185.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.68,
      "end_seconds": 192.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "about nearly five years. Honey and lemon, at night"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.09,
      "end_seconds": 196.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.94,
      "end_seconds": 198.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Six months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.1,
      "end_seconds": 202.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.58,
      "end_seconds": 204.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.46,
      "end_seconds": 210.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.69,
      "end_seconds": 215.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.25,
      "end_seconds": 222.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.19,
      "end_seconds": 226.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.53,
      "end_seconds": 240.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "your chest is clear and your oxygen is normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.06,
      "end_seconds": 259.26,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "please sit back down so, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards acute viral bronchitis i want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.9,
      "end_seconds": 265.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "um, is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.66,
      "end_seconds": 274.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to to an emergency. It looks like acute viral bronchitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.87,
      "end_seconds": 297.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "antibiotics will not help; fluids, rest and honey are best and the cough can last three weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.31,
      "end_seconds": 308.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. We'll catch up if not better in three weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.57,
      "end_seconds": 312.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.76,
      "end_seconds": 316.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Right, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
